# Resume bullets

Each number is generated from the linked result file (`make paper`) and is **`sim`** (digital twin, synthetic human videos). No `real` bullet exists until the queued real-robot sessions are run. Then the real numbers and trial videos (`data/private/sessions/…`, face-free montage) replace these.

- **Built Tidy, an open video-to-robot learning system for a ~{{const.budget_usd}} SO-100-class arm.** It covers phone-video perception, hand→gripper retargeting, ACT policies, uncertainty-driven demo requests and per-step recovery, behind a code-enforced safety layer tested in CI. A measured-state safety audit found {{safety.incidents}} limit violations in {{safety.ticks}} control ticks. `sim` — [`results/sim/safety_audit.json`](results/sim/safety_audit.json)
- **Learned desk clearing from {{const.n_videos}} phone videos with zero teleoperation**, reaching {{m4.video_10.all}} full-chore success vs {{m4.teleop_1x.all}} for a teleop-trained policy at equal human time ({{m4.video_10.min}} vs {{m4.teleop_1x.min}} min). It also beat teleop given 4× the time ({{m4.teleop_4x.all}}). `sim` — [`results/sim/m4_video_vs_teleop_desk_clearing.json`](results/sim/m4_video_vs_teleop_desk_clearing.json)
- **Diagnosed and fixed a silent failure of ACT-style temporal ensembling with delta actions** (chunks encoded the demonstrator's timing, so a lagging arm descended centimetres short). Switching to spatial-target chunks and object-relative observations raised validation item placement from {{dev.video_10|delta_rel}} to {{dev.video_10|cumulative_minimal (default)}}. `sim` — [`results/sim/dev_policy_design_desk_clearing.json`](results/sim/dev_policy_design_desk_clearing.json)
- **Showed embodiment-aware retargeting is essential.** Raw hand trajectories gave {{m4.video_raw.all}} and hand-only (non-object-centric) targets gave {{m4.video_hand.all}}, vs {{m4.video_10.all}} for the full pipeline. Video processing reached grasp/release F1 {{m3.desk_clearing.f1}} and {{m3.desk_clearing.pick}} median object error. `sim` — [`results/sim/m3_perception.json`](results/sim/m3_perception.json)
- **Ran a controlled active-learning study** (uncertainty vs random vs round-robin video requests, {{const.seeds}} seeds). Uncertainty-driven requests did not beat random ({{m5.diff.pooled.uncertainty_random}}), and this is reported as a negative result. `sim` — [`results/sim/m5_active_desk_clearing.json`](results/sim/m5_active_desk_clearing.json)
- **Added learned per-step failure detection with safe retreat and retry** (detector precision {{m6.det.test.prec}}, recall {{m6.det.test.rec}}). Full-chore success went from {{m6.no_recovery}} to {{m6.recovery}}. `sim` — [`results/sim/m6_recovery_desk_clearing.json`](results/sim/m6_recovery_desk_clearing.json)
